.0,0.1145],[475.0,0.2776],[480.0,0.4249],[485.0,0.5541],[490.0,0.6634],[495.0,0.7418],[500.0,0.7907],[505.0,0.838],[510.0,0.8853],[515.0,0.9326],[520.0,0.981],[525.0,1.0428],[530.0,1.1302],[535.0,1.2162],[540.0,1.2913],[545.0,1.3506],[550.0,1.3877],[555.0,1.3973],[560.0,1.3622],[565.0,1.2765],[570.0,1.1424],[575.0,0.964],[580.0,0.7958],[585.0,0.5208],[590.0,0.1276],[595.0,-0.2268],[600.0,-0.2699]],"r":[[555.0,-0.0603],[560.0,-0.0595],[565.0,0.0441],[570.0,0.1508],[575.0,0.2553],[580.0,0.3594],[585.0,0.4622],[590.0,0.5609],[595.0,0.6264],[600.0,0.6819],[605.0,0.7361],[610.0,0.7902],[615.0,0.8446],[620.0,0.9013],[625.0,0.9595],[630.0,1.0274],[635.0,1.112],[640.0,1.1987],[645.0,1.2755],[650.0,1.3303],[655.0,1.3516],[660.0,1.3105],[665.0,1.1784],[670.0,0.93],[675.0,0.6918],[680.0,0.4683],[685.0,0.2545],[690.0,0.0799],[695.0,-0.0325],[700.0,-0.0904]]},"source":{"document":"AF3-0261E","date":"2022-02","file":"fuji-fujifilm-200.pdf","url":"https://asset.fujifilm.com/www/br/files/2025-08/d66a1454a7c1a645947647e52730a2ab/fujifilm-200-speed-film_data-sheet.pdf","sha256":"afd2ef317d21e119545b4401f10b6438312f61dcab82e28ee609724a8b0dcc02"},"notes":["FUJIFILM 200 Color Negative Film (current product; the bulletin compares its processing and printing with Fujicolor C200), Product Information Bulletin, plots on page 5 (nos. 15, 16 and 17); the drawings are vector paths, traced end to end. Issue date 09 FEB 2022 as printed. Process printed on the plots: CN-16 (the bulletin also allows CN-16Q/FA/L/S and Process C-41). Sheet id fuji-200, PDF fuji-fujifilm-200.pdf.","Speed: daylight ISO 200/24 degrees; 3200 K tungsten ISO 50/18 degrees with Wratten 80A (Fuji LBB-12). No Log H Ref and no RMS granularity value is printed in this bulletin (log_h_ref and grain null). The bulletin says processing and printing are almost the same as for C200.","curves: x is log H in lux-seconds as printed (daylight, 1/125 s); all three curves are solid and never touch (D-min plateaus about 0.82 b, 0.37 g, 0.13 r; the curves end at log H about 0.27 b, 0.37 g, 0.33 r). The last point of a line can lie up to one 0.05 step beyond the drawn end (flat extrapolation by the tool).","sensitivity: the y axis has NO numbers, only a double arrow marking 1.0 between two horizontal rules. y is therefore set to 1.0 on the upper rule and 0.0 on the lower rule: the zero is arbitrary, only differences between points and between layers are meaningful. Sensitivity = reciprocal of the exposure in J/cm2 giving density 1.0 above D-min (Status M, CN-16). The blue-sensitive curve is wavy (small bumps near 430 and 450 nm) before its peak at about 470 nm.","sensitivity: each layer ends in a steep drop (blue ends about 495 nm, green starts about 462 nm and ends about 600 nm, red starts about 558 nm and ends about 700 nm); the tool keeps one y per x, so the last few nm of the drops are approximated, and the first/last sample on the 5 nm grid can be a flat extension of up to 5 nm.","dyes: the plot is not of separate cyan/magenta/yellow dyes but of two curves, Mid-scale Density (mid; typical densities for a mid-scale neutral subject) and Minimum Density (min; D-min), 400-720 nm, y = spectral diffuse density as printed (0-2.5)."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier"}